{"created": "2026-09-16T09:36:26.413556+00:00", "modified": "2026-09-16T09:36:26.758577+00:00", "id": 22792358, "conceptrecid": "22734467", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22792358", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22734467", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22792358", "metadata": {"title": "A Strongly Aperiodic Monotile in Three Dimensions", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22792358", "publication_date": "2026-09-16", "description": "<p>We exhibit a rational polyhedral 3-ball, Chair44 (R44), that tiles Euclidean three-space by congruent copies while every such tiling has no nonzero translation period and has a symmetry group of order at most 24. Every tiling is homochiral and carries a unique infinite hierarchy of nested supertiles.</p>\n<p>The tile is a seven-cube chair whose exposed panels carry small rational square-pyramid features. The proof combines written geometry with exhaustive finite enumerations, independent replay implementations, and a Lean 4 formalization. The decisive finite result is that the tile's admitted parent contact language, after rescaling, is exactly its original 44-contact language.</p>\n<p>The accompanying repository provides the exact solid, certificates, verification code, formal development, paper source, viewer, simulations, and reader utilities:<br><a href=\"https://github.com/ioannist/six-birds-tiles\">https://github.com/ioannist/six-birds-tiles</a></p>\n<p><strong>Cryptographic release checkpoint (15 September 2026).</strong> The repository source is sealed by the parentless Git commit <code>137e46b15d36266c37879478cfc62af6e4469147</code>, with root tree <code>b7882f5054ba9f0e56a1a26078d651e75b347728</code> and signed <code>paper-v1</code> tag object <code>9134e6a07fc1d6cb1f3ed5bf0aacbbe6d8cb7da3</code>. The signed external release manifest has SHA-256 <code>9f9b73d115cf34991e8100e255cf3c6cc0485d1a3004b188e0657c036715613e</code> and is recorded in the Sigstore transparency log at Rekor index <code>2841963304</code>. An OpenTimestamps commitment has also been submitted. The verification files accompany the release artifacts.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Tsiokos, Ioannis", "affiliation": "Automorph Inc.", "orcid": "0009-0009-7659-5964"}], "keywords": ["aperiodic monotile", "einstein problem", "strongly aperiodic tilings", "three-dimensional tilings", "polyhedral tiles", "substitution tilings", "hierarchical tilings", "limit-periodic model sets", "computer-assisted proof", "Lean 4", "Six Birds Theory", "emergence calculus"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.1002/j.1538-7305.1961.tb03975.x", "relation": "cites", "resource_type": "publication-article", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1090/memo/0066", "relation": "cites", "resource_type": "publication-book", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1007/BF01418780", "relation": "cites", "resource_type": "publication-article", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://www.archim.org.uk/eureka/archive/Eureka-39.pdf#page=19", "relation": "cites", "resource_type": "publication-article", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "10.1007/978-94-015-8784-6_18", "relation": "cites", "resource_type": "publication-section", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "978-0-486-46981-2", "relation": "cites", "resource_type": "publication-book", "scheme": "isbn"}, {"identifier": "10.1090/S0002-9904-1902-00923-3", "relation": "cites", "resource_type": "publication-article", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zur_Zerlegung_der_euklidischen_R%C3%A4ume_in_kongruente_Polytope_Reinhardt_1928.pdf", "relation": "cites", "resource_type": "publication-article", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "10.1007/BF00239998", "relation": "cites", "resource_type": "publication-article", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "978-0-521-37259-6", "relation": "cites", "resource_type": "publication-book", "scheme": "isbn"}, {"identifier": "10.1016/0012-365X(89)90282-3", "relation": "cites", "resource_type": "publication-article", "scheme": "doi